    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present to the market No 5 Station Court Way. Ideally located on the top floor of this modern development just off The Clonsilla Road this bright and spacious one bedroom apartment has been very well maintained and comes to the market in turnkey condition. \n\nStation Court is a mature and sought-after development of apartments and townhouses built in 2003 by Castlethorn Construction who are renowned builders in Ireland. Number 5 Station Court Way is less than a five-minute walk from Coolmine Train Station which is on the Dublin to Maynooth train line. \n\nThe property shares its entrance with just one other property and is very private. The accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall with hot-press, there is also a 'Stira' stairs leading to a large attic which is partly floored with a light and offers excellent storage. The living room to the front is very well proportioned and has triple glazed double doors leading to a private South/East facing terrace with nice views over the communal grounds. The living room is open plan to the newly fitted kitchen/breakfast room that is fitted with all modern appliances. The kitchen features a range of modern fitted wall and floor units and there is plumbing for a dishwasher and washing machine. The large double bedroom has fully fitted wardrobes. The shower room is fully tiled, this completes the accommodation. \nProximity to Coolmine Train Station ensures this is a most convenient location and will no doubt appeal to the commuter. Blanchardstown Shopping Centre offers a range of shopping and leisure facilities. There are National & Secondary Schools nearby and there are several sporting clubs and excellent golf courses within easy reach. The property also has easy access to the M50 which is only a short drive away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.87m x 1.01m\nWith Hot-Press, access hatch with 'Stira' to large attic space with excellent storage (partly floored with a light).\n\nLiving Room - \nBright living room that is open plan to kitchen area. Laminate timber flooring. Double doors lead to the private paved terrace. PVC French doors with side windows open out to a private South/East facing terrace.\n\nBalcony - \nPaved roof terrace with a sunny South/East facing aspect.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast room - 7.00m x 3.84m\nFully fitted kitchen with a good range of floor and eye level storage units. Integrated oven, gas hob and extractor fan. Plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. (all appliances are included in the sale washing machine, dishwasher, fridge/freezer). Tiled splashback and laminate timber flooing. Open plan to living room.\n\nBedroom - 3.06m x 3.84m\nLarge double bedroom with fully fitted wardrobes and laminate timber flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.93m x 2.83m\nThis recently refurbished shower room is fully tiled and contains a large shower with a rain shower head and hand-held attachment, WC, vanity unit with underneath storage. Heated towel rail. Aquaclad ceiling panels fitted with recessed lighting. Extractor fan.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Top floor apartment</li><li>GFCH</li><li>Private South/East facing terrace</li><li>Five-minute walk to Coolmine Train Station</li><li>Choice of bus routes on Clonsilla Road</li><li>Turnkey condition throughout</li><li>Mature landscaped communal gardens</li><li>Communal parking</ul>"
      },
